   "lines": [
    {
     "n": 1,
     "text": "",
     "end": "space"
    },
    {
     "n": 2,
     "text": "56. We live on alms, cover ourselves with the directions",
     "end": "space"
    },
    {
     "n": 3,
     "text": "serving as garments, and lie down on the surface of the earth:",
     "end": "space"
    },
    {
     "n": 4,
     "text": "what have we to do with big folks ?",
     "end": "space"
    }
   ],
   "uncertain": false,
   "note": null
  },
  {
   "id": "r6",
   "type": "translated_stanza",
   "lines": [
    {
     "n": 1,
     "text": "57. Of what value, indeed, are we in a royal palace since",
     "end": "space"
    },
    {
     "n": 2,
     "text": "we are neither actors, nor flatterers, nor singers; nor have",
     "end": "space"
    },
    {
     "n": 3,
     "text": "we our hearts set on hating others; nor are we ( beautiful )",
     "end": "space"
    },
    {
     "n": 4,
     "text": "women bent down with the burden of the breasts ?",
     "end": "space"
    }
   ],
   "uncertain": false,
   "note": null
  },
  {
   "id": "r7",
   "type": "translated_stanza",
   "lines": [
    {
     "n": 1,
     "text": "58. The world was formerly created by certain large-",
     "end": "hyphen"
    },
    {
     "n": 2,
     "text": "hearted blessed persons; by some it was sustained, and by",
     "end": "space"
    },
    {
     "n": 3,
     "text": "others it was conquered and given away as if it were grass;",
     "end": "space"
    },
    {
     "n": 4,
     "text": "other noble persons even now rule the fourteen worlds.",
     "end": "space"
    },
    {
     "n": 5,
     "text": "What morbid infatuation is it on the part of men when they",
     "end": "space"
    },
    {
     "n": 6,
     "text": "have acquired rulership over a few towns ?",
     "end": "space"
    }
   ],
   "uncertain": false,
   "note": null
  },
  {
   "id": "r8",
   "type": "translated_stanza",
   "lines": [
    {
     "n": 1,
     "text": "59. What honour is it to kings to obtain ( the rulership",
     "end": "space"
    },
    {
     "n": 2,
     "text": "of ) the earth, which was not left unenjoyed even for a mo-",
     "end": "hyphen"
    },
    {
     "n": 3,
     "text": "ment by hundreds of kings; but the lords of a part of its",
     "end": "space"
    },
    {
     "n": 4,
     "text": "( earth's ) part, and of even a small part of that part—fools",
     "end": "space"
    }
   ],
